    "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
    "body": "Many customers especially on ecommerce don't use bundlers, and they don't get dev warnings. And this must be something more than a warning, because it will definitely screw the analysis. However, I don't think it's something the API should \"reject\", because on their end, they just receive a string `\"null\"` which they just cannot reject or ignore. It's on our side to send a correct one, IMO.",
    "commit_id": "5ad000a5aaee59d3ea38bdf363e0d293172a66ac",
    "created_at": "2020-12-01T10:52:28Z",
    "diff_hunk": "@@ -78,18 +94,23 @@ const connectConfigure: ConfigureConnector = function connectConfigure(\n \n     function refine(helper: AlgoliaSearchHelper): Refine {\n       return (searchParameters: PlainSearchParameters) => {\n+        const newSearchParameters = excludeInvalidUserToken(searchParameters);",
